      "argument": [
        {
          "id": "S001",
          "text": "Fix a smooth real mean-zero initial datum and tau>0. All products and Fourier multipliers preserve smoothness and reality. F_tau has P in both terms. H_tau has P in its first term, its second is a scalar mean times S_tau Dinv f, and both endpoint terms have an outer inverse derivative. Thus every iterate stays smooth real and mean zero. At each step take f=S_(-t_n)u^n. Apply E005: v^(n+1)=f+F_n(t_n+tau)+C_n(t_n+tau)-R2_(n,tau)(f,f,f). Here source e^(t partial_x^3)=S_(-t), source A^n=C_n(t_n+tau), and source R2 is D012 with the identical -tau/(18*i*k), covariance and phases. The source physical step agrees term by term with D008-D009, including S_(s-tau) in the last endpoint product.",
          "uses": [
            "E005"
          ],
          "uses_local": [],
          "objects": [
            "tau",
            "f",
            "S",
            "P0",
            "P",
            "Dinv",
            "F_tau",
            "H_tau",
            "Psi",
